The onions in the pan are now soft.
I remember the next instruction from the video.
In the video, the chef says: "First, add a pinch of turmeric."
So, I add a pinch of turmeric to the pan.
After that, he says: "Now mix the soft poha."
I put the soaked poha into the pan.
I also add the roasted peanuts to the pan.
I mix everything well with a large spoon.
The white poha slowly becomes yellow.
Then, I add one spoon of salt.
The next instruction is: "Cover the pan for two minutes."
I put a lid on the pan.
The poha cooks in the steam on low heat.
Two minutes later, I remove the lid.
A very good smell comes from the hot poha.
Now this dish is almost ready.
I squeeze half a lemon over it.
Finally, I put fresh green coriander on top.
My Kande Pohe are completely ready!
Now I just wait for Neha and Amit to arrive.
